{"id": "68328f30dd3668c87668", "repository": "michaelshimeles/rstack", "commit_sha": "11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7", "skill_path": "before-and-after/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/michaelshimeles/rstack/blob/11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7/before-and-after/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "fc9c51c4d73bcd3efa320a550ebe3a2f363bb82a", "sha256": "df52809f5ac11adbdeae6b94394df14c8babacfc4dbe1fb1684bb474838b9bfa", "bytes": 4535, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:43:24.684798+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/michaelshimeles/rstack/11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7/before-and-after/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": ["before-and-after/LICENSE"], "repository_manifest": "manifests/michaelshimeles/rstack/11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7.json", "local_package_files": ["before-and-after/LICENSE", "before-and-after/SKILL.md", "before-and-after/scripts/adapters/0x0st.sh", "before-and-after/scripts/adapters/blob.sh", "before-and-after/scripts/upload-and-copy.sh"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: before-and-after\ndescription: Captures before/after screenshots of web pages or elements for visual comparison. Use when user says \"take before and after\", \"screenshot comparison\", \"visual diff\", \"PR screenshots\", \"compare old and new\", or needs to document UI changes. Accepts two URLs (file://, http://, https://) or two image paths.\nallowed-tools:\n  - Bash(npx @vercel/before-and-after *)\n  - Bash(before-and-after *)\n  - Bash(which before-and-after)\n  - Bash(npm install -g @vercel/before-and-after)\n  - Bash(*/upload-and-copy.sh *)\n  - Bash(curl -s -o /dev/null -w *)\n  - Bash(gh pr view *)\n  - Bash(gh pr edit *)\n  - Bash(vercel inspect *)\n  - Bash(vercel whoami)\n  - Bash(which vercel)\n  - Bash(which gh)", "declared_name": "before-and-after", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "0b0ef693da7cacd3953d", "repository": "michaelshimeles/rstack", "commit_sha": "11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7", "skill_path": "code-structure/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/michaelshimeles/rstack/blob/11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7/code-structure/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "1317e82f9f8b019c775d0b54f8c9a9f73dcfd121", "sha256": "aa2e0e88c3b3714898236d5f65e4102e21b43747de99ae503dfc15102aae6ba4", "bytes": 5060, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:43:24.685275+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/michaelshimeles/rstack/11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7/code-structure/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/michaelshimeles/rstack/11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7.json", "local_package_files": ["code-structure/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: code-structure\ndescription: Use when multiple workflows duplicate the same operational logic, when deciding what belongs in actions vs shared services, or when refactoring repeated operational blocks across domain flows. Use when adding new features that share mechanics with existing ones.", "declared_name": "code-structure", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "7c9e8900b85820693373", "repository": "michaelshimeles/rstack", "commit_sha": "11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7", "skill_path": "evidence-driven-testing/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/michaelshimeles/rstack/blob/11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7/evidence-driven-testing/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "97f670972ec393d3599c9fa5a97f884242a54b40", "sha256": "c5800269a6abb10d6da63b468e6112082dea3b9b38077b9e1f32fa8151e3752c", "bytes": 16932, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:43:24.685353+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/michaelshimeles/rstack/11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7/evidence-driven-testing/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/michaelshimeles/rstack/11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7.json", "local_package_files": ["evidence-driven-testing/SKILL.md", "evidence-driven-testing/scripts/evidence.py", "evidence-driven-testing/scripts/playwright/package-lock.json", "evidence-driven-testing/scripts/playwright/package.json", "evidence-driven-testing/scripts/run-playwright.sh"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: evidence-driven-testing\ndescription: >\n  Records visual proof while testing UI behavior — the agent tests the app\n  hands-on via computer use while a screen recording with structured\n  test/assertion annotations captures the session — then posts the video and a\n  results summary to the requested destination. Use when changed runtime\n  behavior needs observable verification, including\n  headless environments (scripted screenshots and probes) and non-UI changes\n  (measured numbers, output pairs).\ncompatibility: Screen-recording path requires a GUI environment the agent can drive — built-in computer use, or the cua-driver CLI (trycua/cua) when the harness has no computer-use tools — plus an authenticated browser session for the app under test. The bundled recorder (scripts/evidence.py) runs on Linux (X11 via x11grab, Wayland via wf-recorder), macOS (avfoundation, needs Screen Recording permission) and Windows (gdigrab) and needs Python 3 plus ffmpeg + ffprobe built with libx264 and the ass filter. The headless helper requires Bash, Node 20+, npm, and Chromium system libraries; it installs Playwright outside the target project. Posting evidence requires gh (GitHub CLI) or equivalent.\nmetadata:\n  version: \"1.2\"", "declared_name": "evidence-driven-testing", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
